ALGORITHM: STRASSEN-MATRIX-MULTIPLICATION(A, B, n)

1. If n = 1
      C[0][0] = A[0][0] × B[0][0]
      Return C

2. Divide A into four sub-matrices:
      A11, A12, A21, A22

3. Divide B into four sub-matrices:
      B11, B12, B21, B22

4. Calculate:
      M1 = (A11 + A22)(B11 + B22)
      M2 = (A21 + A22)B11
      M3 = A11(B12 - B22)
      M4 = A22(B21 - B11)
      M5 = (A11 + A12)B22
      M6 = (A21 - A11)(B11 + B12)
      M7 = (A12 - A22)(B21 + B22)

5. Calculate the four parts of C:
      C11 = M1 + M4 - M5 + M7
      C12 = M3 + M5
      C21 = M2 + M4
      C22 = M1 - M2 + M3 + M6

6. Combine C11, C12, C21 and C22.

7. Return C.


TIME COMPLEXITY
T(n) = 7T(n/2) + O(n^2)

Therefore,
T(n) = O(n^log2(7))
T(n) = O(n^2.807)
